<title>USA: FSA qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following five municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Paris School District No 7, Ark., $2.44 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--St Ansgar Community School District, Iowa, $3.334 million general obligation school bonds.</p>
<p>--Avalon Borough, N.J., $11.4 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Seaford Union Free School District, N.Y., $5 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Akron, Ohio, $6.31 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
